Body:
Nice request — first-party QwenCloud would be cleaner for discovery.

Until it lands, the international DashScope compatible endpoint already works as a custom OpenAI-compatible provider in `opencode.json` (same pattern as other openai-compatible APIs in the providers docs):

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "qwencloud": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "QwenCloud International",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1"
      },
      "models": {
        "qwen3.8-max": { "name": "Qwen3.8 Max" },
        "qwen3.7-plus": { "name": "Qwen3.7 Plus" },
        "qwen3.7-flash": { "name": "Qwen3.7 Flash" },
        "qwen3.6-omni-plus": { "name": "Qwen3.6 Omni Plus" }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Then set `QWENCLOUD_API_KEY` / DashScope key via `opencode auth` (or env) and pick `qwencloud/<model-id>`.

Model IDs can drift — confirm against current QwenCloud docs before pinning. Glad to see #43674-style work getting revived with the PR template + models.dev catalog piece.

Adding a **self-contained** repro that needs no captured traffic — only the trigger condition (a delta carrying `reasoning_content` together with an empty `tool_calls: []` array, which is what DeepSeek/llama.cpp-style streams emit on every reasoning chunk).

```bash
npm i ai@6 @ai-sdk/openai-compatible@2.0.41   # rerun with @2.0.75
```

`repro.mjs`:

```js
import { createOpenAICompatible } from "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible"
import { streamText } from "ai"
import { createRequire } from "node:module"

const require = createRequire(import.meta.url)
const pkgVersion = require("@ai-sdk/openai-compatible/package.json").version

const TOKENS = ["We", " need", " to", " think", " first"]
const sse = TOKENS.map(
  (t) =>
    `data: ${JSON.stringify({
      id: "chatcmpl-test",
      object: "chat.completion.chunk",
      choices: [
        {
          index: 0,
          delta: { role: "assistant", content: "", reasoning_content: t, tool_calls: [] },
          finish_reason: null,
        },
      ],
    })}`,
).concat([
  `data: ${JSON.stringify({
    id: "chatcmpl-test",
    object: "chat.completion.chunk",
    choices: [{ index: 0, delta: { content: "Because of Rayleigh scattering." }, finish_reason: "stop" }],
  })}`,
])

const fetchMock = async () =>
  new Response(
    new ReadableStream({
      async start(ctl) {
        for (const line of sse) ctl.enqueue(new TextEncoder().encode(line + "\n\n"))
        ctl.enqueue(new TextEncoder().encode("data: [DONE]\n\n"))
        ctl.close()
      },
    }),
    { status: 200, headers: { "content-type": "text/event-stream" } },
  )

const provider = createOpenAICompatible({ name: "replay", baseURL: "https://replay.local/v1", fetch: fetchMock })

const counts = { "reasoning-start": 0, "reasoning-delta": 0, "reasoning-end": 0, "text-delta": 0, finish: 0 }
const result = streamText({ model: provider.chatModel("test-model"), prompt: "hi" })
for await (const part of result.fullStream) if (part.type in counts) counts[part.type]++

console.log(`@ai-sdk/openai-compatible@${pkgVersion} + ai@${require("ai/package.json").version}`)
console.log(`  reasoning tokens sent: ${TOKENS.length}`)
console.log(`  ${JSON.stringify(counts)}`)
```

Output — **identical `ai@6.0.286` core, only the provider differs**:

`@ai-sdk/openai-compatible@2.0.41`:
```
reasoning tokens sent: 5
{"reasoning-start":5,"reasoning-delta":5,"reasoning-end":5,"text-delta":1,"finish":1}
```

`@ai-sdk/openai-compatible@2.0.75`:
```
reasoning tokens sent: 5
{"reasoning-start":1,"reasoning-delta":5,"reasoning-end":1,"text-delta":1,"finish":1}
```

I also replayed a real captured DeepSeek stream (268 reasoning tokens, each delta carrying `tool_calls: []`):
- `2.0.41` → `reasoning-start:268 / reasoning-end:268`
- `2.0.75` → `reasoning-start:1 / reasoning-end:1`

Both confirm the fix already present in `2.0.75` (`f3c1980` — "keep reasoning streams contiguous when deltas include empty tool call arrays") is exactly what un-fragments these streams. Bumping the bundled version from `2.0.41` to `2.0.75` resolves it without touching the AI SDK 6 core.
